# Which windows exist at startup, and where.
#
# Each line is a PATH — the type is inferred from content and the role
# derived from permissions, so a layout never says what a thing is.
# Indentation NESTS; the axis is not stated because alternation already
# determines it. `tabs` is the only keyword: its children share one
# rectangle.
#
# A role may be appended when the derived default is not what you meant.
# `manage` on an executable RUNS it, and the window is `shell` on the
# resulting channel — which is the whole of "open a terminal".

/                       manage
tabs
    /etc/motd
    /rc/tour
    /home/README
/bin/rc                 manage
